{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_41","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,220p' /Users/stuart/.darkfactory/openspec/changes/dispatch-test-coverage/tasks.md\"","aggregated_output":"## 1. Parser table tests\n\n- [x] 1.1 Add table-driven tests for parse_codex_event covering all event types: thread.started, item.started (tool_use, function_call, agent_message), item.completed (agent_message, tool_use, file write, file read), turn.completed (with token usage), turn.failed, error, empty line, non-JSON line, unknown JSON type. Each test provides a real NDJSON line and asserts the correct EventKind and extracted fields. Add as inline #[cfg(test)] in src/engine.rs.\n\n## 2. Engine error path tests\n\n- [ ] 2.1 Add engine integration tests for: (a) spawn failure with missing binary (set PATH to empty, expect BinaryNotFound or SpawnFailed), (b) failed child with non-zero exit (mock script that exits 1, assert status Failed with exit_code), (c) missing output (mock script that succeeds but doesn't write -o file, assert missing_output error), (d) soft timeout where child respects SIGTERM (mock with short timeout, assert TimedOut status and child is dead). Add to tests/engine.rs.\n\n## 3. Timeout math and grace tests\n\n- [ ] 3.1 Add unit tests for effective_grace_sec: (a) grace=0 with timeout=900 -> 450, (b) grace=0 with timeout=1 -> 1 (minimum), (c) grace=0 with timeout=0 -> 1 (minimum), (d) explicit grace=30 passes through unchanged. Add as inline #[cfg(test)] in src/engine.rs.\n\n## 4. Lifecycle negative path tests\n\n- [ ] 4.1 Add CLI integration tests for: (a) status with unknown dispatch ID exits non-zero, (b) result with unknown ID exits non-zero, (c) wait with unknown ID exits non-zero, (d) status with corrupt status.json handles gracefully, (e) result with corrupt result.json handles gracefully. Add to tests/cli.rs.\n\n## 5. Supervisor edge case tests\n\n- [ ] 5.1 Add supervisor tests for: (a) spawn with non-existent binary returns error, (b) kill_soft sends SIGTERM (verify child receives signal 15), (c) normal exit reports exit_code with no signal. Add to tests/supervisor.rs.\n\n## 6. Smoke test script\n\n- [ ] 6.1 Create tests/smoketest.sh: a POSIX shell script that builds the release binary, then runs 3 live-codex dispatches: (a) simple task (echo to file), verify completed status and output_exists, (b) timeout test (sleep with 10s timeout), verify timed_out status, (c) prompt-file test (write prompt to temp file, dispatch with --prompt-file), verify completed. Each test prints PASS/FAIL. Script exits non-zero if any test fails. Add a `smoke` target to the Makefile that runs this script.\n\n## 7. Closing tasks\n\n- [ ] 7.1 Cleanup: verify `make check` passes (fmt + clippy + all tests). Remove any dead test helpers or unused imports introduced during test writing.\n- [ ] 7.2 Documentation: update CLAUDE.md testing table if test file structure changed. Verify test count increased from 35.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"tool_end","dispatch_id":"01KQ3Z2S6JP5RME7VCFR7PVGT4","ts":"2026-04-26T04:02:49Z","tool":"command_execution"}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_42","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,220p' /Users/stuart/.darkfactory/openspec/changes/dispatch-test-coverage/mission/briefs/task-2.md\"","aggregated_output":"# Worker Brief: Task 2 - Engine error path tests\n\n## Your Task\nAdd integration tests in `tests/engine.rs` for four engine error paths that currently have no coverage.\n\n### Tests to write\n\n**1. Spawn failure with missing binary**\nSet PATH to an empty/nonexistent directory so `codex` can't be found. Call `engine::dispatch(...)`. Assert it returns an error (DispatchError::SpawnFailed or similar), not a hang or panic.\n\nPattern: Use the existing `TestPath` helper if available, or temporarily set PATH. The key is that the dispatch function returns a clean error.\n\n**2. Failed child with non-zero exit**\nCreate a mock script that exits with code 1:\n```bash\n#!/bin/bash\necho '{\"type\":\"thread.started\",\"thread_id\":\"fail-test\"}'\necho '{\"type\":\"turn.completed\",\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":10,\"output_tokens\":5,\"reasoning_tokens\":0}}'\nexit 1\n```\nDispatch with this mock as the \"codex\" binary. Assert:\n- `result.status == DispatchStatus::Failed`\n- `result.exit_code == Some(1)`\n- `result.signal == None`\n\n**3. Missing output file (exit 0 but no -o file)**\nCreate a mock script that exits 0 but doesn't write the output file:\n```bash\n#!/bin/bash\necho '{\"type\":\"thread.started\",\"thread_id\":\"no-output\"}'\necho '{\"type\":\"turn.completed\",\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":10,\"output_tokens\":5,\"reasoning_tokens\":0}}'\nexit 0\n```\nDispatch with `--output /tmp/nonexistent-output.md`. Assert:\n- `result.status == DispatchStatus::Failed` (or whatever status the engine uses)\n- `result.output_exists == false`\n- `result.error` contains \"missing_output\" or similar\n\n**4. Soft timeout where child respects SIGTERM**\nCreate a mock script that runs for a while but exits cleanly on SIGTERM:\n```bash\n#!/bin/bash\ntrap 'exit 0' TERM\nsleep 300\n```\nDispatch with timeout=1, grace=5. The child should receive SIGTERM at soft timeout and exit. Assert:\n- `result.status == DispatchStatus::TimedOut`\n- The child process is dead (verify with kill -0)\n\n### Code standards\n- Read `tools/darkfactory-dispatch/CLAUDE.md`\n- Follow the existing test patterns in tests/engine.rs\n- Use `#[tokio::test(flavor = \"multi_thread\")]` for async tests\n- Verify `cargo test` passes after adding\n\n## What Previous Tasks Built\n- tests/engine.rs already has: successful_dispatch, timeout_dispatch, heartbeat, malformed_ndjson tests\n- tests/test_codex_mock.sh is used as a mock codex binary\n- The TestPath helper (if it exists) swaps the codex binary on PATH for tests\n\n## Procedures\n- Read existing tests/engine.rs to understand the test patterns and helpers\n- Add the 4 new tests\n- Create any needed mock scripts in tests/\n- Verify `cargo test` passes\n- Commit: \"[test-2] Add engine error path tests for spawn failure, failed child, missing output, and SIGTERM timeout\"\n- Write handoff to openspec/changes/dispatch-test-coverage/mission/handoffs/task-2.md\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
